.TH RUWAC 1 "2026-10-17" "RUWAC" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ruwac \- persistent terminal multiplexer and remote workspace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ruwac \-S
.I NAME
.br
.B ruwac \-r
.I NAME_OR_SESSION_ID
.br
.B ruwac \-ls
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B ruwac kill-session
.I NAME_OR_SESSION_ID
.br
.B ruwac gui
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
RUWAC keeps terminals in a headless daemon. Closing a client detaches its
view while programs continue running. Several clients may share a session
with independent focus. The optional GTK desktop provides terminal, SSH,
RDP, machine-bookmark, file-transfer and coding-agent views.
.PP
Detachment does not provide process survival across a reboot or daemon
termination. Saved history and workspace layouts are distinct from live
processes. RDP transports currently belong to the desktop process.
.SH BASIC COMMANDS
.TP
.B engine status
Report installed CLI and running engine versions without starting a daemon.
With \-\-host, discovery runs through an updated CLI on that SSH endpoint.
.TP
.B engine gui
Open an independent GUI window on a separate updated engine. Preserve the
original engine, terminals and saved workspace; no sessions are migrated.
.TP
.B engine new
Start or reuse the separate engine and print JSON launch argument arrays.
Retain both RUWAC_SOCKET and RUWAC_STATE_FILE from these arrays when reconnecting.
An existing custom RUWAC_STATE_FILE must be unset before using this command.
.TP
.BI "\-S " NAME
Create and attach a named session, or attach the existing exact name.
Starts the daemon when required.
.TP
.BI "\-r " NAME_OR_SESSION_ID
Reattach only. Duplicate names are refused; use the full ID from \-ls.
.TP
.BI "\-x " NAME
Attach an existing session for shared access.
.TP
.BI "\-R " NAME
Attach or create a named session.
.TP
.BI "\-dmS " NAME
Create a detached session.
.TP
.B \-ls
List persistent sessions, window counts, state and exact IDs.
.TP
.BI "\-wipe " "[NAME_OR_SESSION_ID] [\-\-json]"
Remove dead windows and sessions. With a name or ID, restrict cleanup to that
exact session. Preserve every window containing a live process.
.TP
.BI "kill-session " NAME_OR_SESSION_ID
End all programs in only the selected session. This is destructive.
.TP
.BI "attach \-\-session " SESSION_ID
Explicit attachment syntax, also usable by older clients.
.TP
.BI "pane list \-\-session " SESSION_ID " \-\-json"
List panes, process IDs and ended/restored state.
.SH TERMINAL KEYS
The CLI prefix is Ctrl+A. Press the prefix, then a command key.
.TP
.B d
Detach; programs continue.
.TP
.B c
New terminal window.
.TP
.B n / p
Next / previous window.
.TP
.B 0 through 9
Select a window. Alt+digits also selects windows in the CLI.
.TP
.B s / |
Split horizontally / vertically.
.TP
.B Tab / z
Change pane / toggle zoom.
.TP
.B [ / ]
Selection/history mode / paste internal buffer.
.TP
.B a
Send literal prefix to the application. Repeated prefixes support nesting.
.PP
The clickable bottom bar selects windows. In a shell, scrolling enters
history, dragging selects and middle-click pastes. Mouse-aware applications
receive their own events. Shift+drag uses the outer terminal selection.
.PP
The native desktop sends Ctrl+A to applications, including nested tmux;
its own control prefix is Ctrl+Alt+A.
.SH DESKTOP KEYS
.TP
.B Alt+M / Alt+A
Open Machines and focus search / open Agents and running agent sessions.
These host menu keys work in either Map keys mode.
.TP
.B Alt+1 through Alt+9 / Alt+0
Select desktop tabs 1 through 10 by default.
.TP
.B AltGr tap
Toggle Map keys. When enabled, Alt+digits and system shortcuts go to the
focused terminal or remote desktop. Holding AltGr with another key remains
normal keyboard-layout input.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+T / Ctrl+Shift+R
New terminal / choose an RDP machine.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Alt+Enter
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Alt+Home
Release remote focus to local controls.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C / Ctrl+Shift+V
Desktop copy / paste.
.SH REMOTE USE
.B ruwac \-\-host SSH_HOST
.I COMMAND
runs the corresponding command over verified SSH. For example:
.PP
.nf
ruwac --host example-host -r development
ruwac --host example-host session list --json
.fi
.PP
SSH and RDP accounts and credential references are independent. Unknown or
changed host identities require review; no password belongs in command-line
arguments. Optional provider installation does not log in to the provider.
.SH UPDATES
.TP
.B update \-\-check
Check published releases.
.TP
.B update \-\-install
Install the newest eligible verified release for the current delivery mode.
Does not restart live sessions or RDP connections.
.TP
.B update \-\-rollback
Select the previous per-user installation. RPM rollback uses its supported
package-management path. See the command output for delivery-specific limits.
.TP
.B update \-\-auto-check on|off|status
Control periodic checks.
.TP
.B update \-\-auto-install on|off|status
Control optional automatic installation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ruwac/
Private daemon sockets and runtime state. An explicit socket's parent must
be owned by the current user with mode 0700.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/RUWAC/
Private machine metadata, desktop settings and saved workspaces. If unset,
XDG_CONFIG_HOME defaults to ~/.config. Passwords are stored in Secret Service.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUWAC_SOCKET
Select a daemon socket. \-\-socket PATH overrides it.
.TP
.B SHELL
Selected login shell for new terminal processes. Existing shells are preserved.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Common Screen commands are supported; the complete GNU Screen language is
not implemented. Current packaged builds target Fedora 44 x86_64. Windows
and macOS native clients are not qualified. External RDP and physical input
coverage varies; a stable version number is not universal interoperability
or security qualification. Consult the source acceptance and security reports.
